BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Wickedgood Candle Return) Tj T* () Tj T* (Wickedgood Candle Return) Tj T* (Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Candles are a popular product, especially as gifts, but when a candle is finished the jar is) Tj T* (usually thrown in the trash. Many candle jars are made of good quality glass that could be used) Tj T* (many more times. Because there is no easy way to send them back, most people either throw them) Tj T* (out or keep a few around the house as storage. This creates unnecessary waste and is a growing) Tj T* (concern for people who care about the environment. At the same time, small candle makers want) Tj T* (to be more sustainable but they are busy making and selling candles. They do not have the time,) Tj T* (space, or money to set up their own system for collecting, cleaning and reusing jars. Customers) Tj T* (who want to do the right thing also have no easy way to see the impact of their choices. We) Tj T* (believe this is a real problem that affects both buyers and sellers of candles.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Wickedgood Candle Return is a reuse program that makes returning candle jars simple. Our) Tj T* (solution has three parts.) Tj T* () Tj T* (First, a prepaid mailer. A candle maker who partners with us includes a prepaid return mailer) Tj T* (in the box with each candle order, or customers can request one from us. When the candle is) Tj T* (finished the customer puts the empty jar in the mailer and drops it in the mail.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Second, cleaning and refilling. When jars arrive at our workspace we remove leftover wax, wash) Tj T* (and sanitize the glass, inspect it for chips and cracks, and then send good jars back to the) Tj T* (candle maker, who refills them with fresh wax and sells them again.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Third, a data dashboard. Each customer and each candle maker can log in to see how many jars) Tj T* (have been returned, how much glass waste was avoided, and an estimate of the carbon saved. We) Tj T* (think this makes the impact feel real and gives candle makers something to share with their own) Tj T* (customers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The candle market is large and growing. Candles are sold in grocery stores, gift shops, online) Tj T* (shops and at craft markets. Our focus is on two groups. The first is eco-minded gift buyers,) Tj T* (who often choose products based on values and are willing to pay a bit more for something) Tj T* (sustainable. The second is small and independent candle makers, who number in the thousands) Tj T* (across the country and sell mostly online and at local markets. We estimate that if even a) Tj T* (small share of these makers joined our program, we could handle a very large number of jars) Tj T* (each year. We have not yet done a detailed market sizing, but we believe the growing interest) Tj T* (in sustainability and reuse means demand will continue to increase.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to make money in a few ways. Candle makers would pay us a fee for each jar that is) Tj T* (returned, cleaned and sent back to them. Customers may also pay a small fee for the mailer when) Tj T* (it is not included by the candle maker. In the future we could offer premium dashboard features) Tj T* (to candle makers, such as more detailed reports they can use in marketing. We have not) Tj T* (finalized our prices. Our early thinking is that a fee per jar would be lower than the cost of) Tj T* (buying new jars, which would make the program attractive to candle makers, but we still need to) Tj T* (test this. Our costs include the mailers, postage, cleaning supplies, labor and the software) Tj T* (for the dashboard. We expect that as we handle more jars our cost per jar will come down.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are other reuse and return programs in the market, and some larger candle brands have) Tj ET
endstream
